ont on the opening backstroke leg, splitting an American record 1:00.82, with Germany second, but 0.79 seconds behind. On the breaststroke leg, Russian " [:a {:href "/athletes/45559"} "Yelena Rudkovskaya"] " finished in 1:07.44, the second fastest ever breaststroke split, which almost caught the USA’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/51136"} "Anita Nall"] ", and moved the Unifieds into second. " [:a {:href "/athletes/50949"} "Crissy Ahmann-Leighton"] " then swam fly for the US, putting the race away, as Germany and the Unified Team settled into second and third. That is how they would finish, " [:a {:href "/athletes/51217"} "Jenny Thompson"] " anchoring the Americans on freestyle for the gold medal, splitting 54.47 for the third-fastest split of all-time. The USA won in 4:02.54, breaking the world record which had been held by an East German team since 1973."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "4:10.83 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "4:02.54 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Backstroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "621"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51103"} "Lea Loveless"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Breaststroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "624"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51136"} "Anita Nall"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Butterfly"] [:td {:class "bib"} "600"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50949"} "Crissy Ahmann-Leighton"] " "] [:td {}] [:t